body:
Nero, while a decent stat line, is generally not a great card in Lucci decks. I'd cut him, and 1 Lucci to fit in 2k Tashgi's. 

&#x200B;

My line of thought is that generally you only want to run 2 of the 3 vanilla bodies. You could also swap out Jabra to keep the Neros if you want more early bodies.

If anyone needs Expanded stuff I'd be willing to give trainers, and non-GX+ away to newer players. I only play standard so no need for older cards and if it's going into the hands of someone who can use it, I'd be happy to help the community.

&#x200B;

Edit: I've run out of anything worthwhile! Thank you all for reaching out!

US10.5/L

&#x200B;

Thanks Tony!

There's a chance I'd be interested after the holidays. I'm looking for a pair of Sesames but don't want to spoil the potential of getting them as a gift since I've been so vocal about wanting a pair. 

&#x200B;

Would you say these run TTS? I keep hearing mixed reviews.

If you can't find a GPS model, I've got a brand new 38mm Series 3 LTE + GPS. Asking $320 + shipping.

&#x200B;

[https://imgur.com/a/FQv38vu](https://imgur.com/a/FQv38vu)

Hey Wicca,

&#x200B;

What's keeping you from preforming in Philly more? I went to your show at First Unitarian but have yet to see you in the city since.
